set-bg: img/map_2.png
new-page: true

> *"The necessity of deliberately allowing and encouraging the instability of society [...] We welcome this social instability because it provides the opportunity to progress. Progress positively demands an element of instability and even of risk."*

 - Roeslan Abdulgani, *Indonesia's National Council: First Year*, 1958

This is a game of alternate history. While historical accuracy is a major concern, keep in mind that this is a *game*, and that any divergence from actual events will necessarily have to involve some element of make-believe. Nevertheless, please let the author know if there are any glaring mistakes.

For more information on the politics and government of the Republic of Indonesia during the Liberal Democratic Era, see the "Library" page on the top left. If this is your first time playing the game, it is strongly recommended that you read at least some of this information.

- @1951_easy: Begin (easy difficulty)
- @1951_main: Begin (normal difficulty) (Not Supported)
- @1951_hard: Begin (hard difficulty) (Not Supported)
- @1951_historical: Begin (historical mode) (Not Supported)

